</div>","contentLength":1127,"flags":null,"enclosureUrl":"","enclosureMime":"","commentsUrl":null},{"title":"The Risk of Exposed Cloud Functions and How to Harden","url":"https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/exposed-cloud-functions-harden/","date":1784124000,"author":"Mandiant","guid":377,"unread":true,"content":"<div><p>Written by: Corné de Jong</p></div><div><ul></ul><h3></h3><h3></h3><ul></ul><h4></h4></div><div><pre><code>import functions_framework\n\n@functions_framework.http\ndef hello_http(request):\n    request_json = request.get_json(silent=True)\n    request_args = request.args\n    if request_json and 'file' in request_json:\n        file = request_json['file']\n    elif request_args and 'file' in request_args:\n        file = request_args['file']\n \n# VULNERABILITY: The 'file' parameter is used directly in open() \n# without validation, allowing arbitrary file access\n    with open(file, 'r') as resp:\n          filedata = resp.read()\n    return 'local file data {}!'.format(filedata)</code></pre></div><div><pre><code>curl -X POST https://cloudrun01-abc.europe-west3.run.app/ -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"file\": \"main.py\"}'</code></pre></div><div><ul></ul></div><div><pre><code>curl -X POST https://cloudrun01-abc.europe-west3.run.app/ -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"file\": \"../../../etc/passwd\"}'</code></pre></div><div><ul><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><code>requirements.txt, package.json, go.mod</code></p></li><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><strong>Application configuration files: </strong></p></li><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><code>/etc/passwd, /proc/self/environ</code></p></li></ul><h4></h4></div><div><pre><code>import functions_framework\nimport subprocess\n\n\n@functions_framework.http\ndef hello_http(request):\n  request_json = request.get_json(silent=True)\n  request_args = request.args\n  if request_json and 'input' in request_json:\n      input = request_json['input']\n  elif request_args and 'input' in request_args:\n      input = request_args['input']\n  result = subprocess.run(input, shell=True,capture_output=True, text=True)\n  return format(result)</code></pre></div><div><pre><code>curl -X POST https://cloudrun02-abc.europe-west3.run.app/ -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d \"{\\\"input\\\": \\\"curl 'http://metadata.google.internal/computeMetadata/v1/instance/service-accounts/default/token' -H 'Metadata-Flavor: Google'\\\"}\"</code></pre></div><div><p><code>CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN</code></p></div><div><pre><code>export CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN=”obtain bearer token”</code></pre></div><div><ul></ul><h3></h3><ul><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><strong>Secure Software Development Lifecycle (S-SDLC): </strong></p></li><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><a href=\"https://www.wiz.io/academy/ai-security/vibe-coding-security\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"></a></p></li><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><strong>Compensating Runtime Controls: </strong></p></li></ul><h4></h4><p><a href=\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/architecture/blueprints/serverless-blueprint\"></a></p><h4></h4><ul><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><strong>Cloud Storage Bucket Access:</strong><code>roles/storage.objectViewer</code></p></li><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><code> Secret Manager Secret Accessor</code><code>roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor</code><a href=\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/secrets#required_roles\"></a></p></li></ul><h4></h4><ul><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><strong>Centralized Traffic Management:</strong></p></li><li aria-level=\"1\"><p role=\"presentation\"><strong>Identity-Aware Proxy (IAP):</strong></p></li></ul><h4></h4><p><a href=\"https://cloud.google.com/security/products/armor\"></a></p></div><div><pre><code>evaluatePreconfiguredWaf('lfi-v33-stable', {'sensitivity': 3})</code></pre></div>